  "body": "## What changed\n\nA typed Slot whose cutter reaches its round caps was reported as a Gouge on every plunge and feed, so it never posted (#510). The cause was the region the verifier checks a Slot against, `operation::material::stadium`. It drew each cap as 16 chords **inscribed** in the true arc. A chord sits up to `h(1 - cos 5.625°)` inside the arc, and the slot generator's passes follow the true arc exactly, so the gouge check (`d(centre, boundary) >= r - GOUGE_TOL`) flagged a cutter that only touched the cap.\n\nThe caps are now the polygon **circumscribed** about the arc. Every chord is tangent to the arc, and the corners sit at `h / cos(phi/2)`. The chord count is set per slot (`cap_segments`) so a corner stands at most `CAP_SAG_BUDGET = 0.001 mm` outside the arc, with 16 to 2048 chords per cap. The first and last corner of each cap lie on the lines of the straight sides, so the sides stay exact. `GOUGE_TOL` is unchanged.\n\n**Posted G-code: unchanged.** The generator is untouched. Only the gouge verdict changes, plus the drawn region outline, which moves by at most 1 µm.\n\n## Readings (80×60×20 stock, EM-0600-4FL, a=(-15,0), b=(15,0), Top 20, Bottom 10, stepdown 5)\n\n| | before | after |\n|---|---|---|\n| width 6 (centreline pass) | `Gouge` at moves 2, 3, 7, 8, 12, 13; post blocked | no warnings; posts |\n| width 10 (rings at ±2) | `Gouge` on all 18 plunges/feeds; post blocked | no warnings; posts |\n| cap-centre distance to boundary (r = 3) | 2.9855 (needs ≥ 2.99) | ≥ 3.0 (tangent) |\n| path pushed +0.05 mm in X past the cap | (already convicted) | still convicted |\n\n## Top-Z pass\n\nThe issue also reports that a Slot makes a feed pass at its Top before stepping down. The other 2D ladders do the same: `cut_levels(top, bottom, step)` starts at Top for pocket, contour, circular, trace, face and the 3D entries. It is an air pass, never a gouge. This PR pins the current behaviour rather than changing one op on its own. The decision file explains why and recommends a separate issue if the first level should be `top - stepdown` for every ladder.\n\n## Tests\n\nNew `crates/app/tests/slot_caps.rs`:\n- `a_slot_riding_its_round_caps_verifies_clean_and_posts`: widths 6 and 10, each run with stock as the source and with a slotted part model as the source. Each run has no Gouge, no warning that blocks posting, and `post_setup` writes the program.\n- `a_slot_driven_past_its_cap_is_still_a_gouge`: the generated path, shifted 0.05 mm past the cap and checked against the op's own `region_of`, is convicted. The unshifted path checks clean.\n- `the_stadium_region_hugs_the_true_caps`: at 721 angles on both caps, the true arc is inside the region and a point 2 µm past it is outside.\n- `the_slot_ladder_starts_at_the_authored_top`: the cut levels are [20, 15, 10].\n\nBefore the fix, the first three fail and the fourth passes.\n\nGate (debug): camcraft-app lib (101), slot_caps, operations, area_controls, cutting_data, project_roundtrip, golden_cl, verify and blind_floor all pass. `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings` is clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The release `--ignored` lanes. No goldens move, because the generator output is unchanged.\n- The UI region-outline drawing (the outline moves by at most 1 µm).\n- Hand-run in the GUI or on a real machine.\n\nDecision file: `docs/decisions/510-slot-cap-region.md`.\n\nChangelog: A typed Slot whose cutter reaches its round ends is no longer falsely reported as a gouge, so it posts again (#510)\n\nFixes #510\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
